# {{.Name}}

A service built on [Muzak](https://muzak.dev).

## Running it

```bash
go mod tidy
go run ./cmd/server
```

Then call it, and read the OpenAPI document it describes itself with:

```bash
curl 'http://localhost:8080/hello?name=you'
curl http://localhost:8080/openapi.json
```

While you work on it, `muzak dev` builds and runs the server, and rebuilds and
restarts it whenever a Go file changes:

```bash
muzak dev
```

## Testing it

```bash
go test ./...
```

The tests serve the application in-process with `muzak.dev/framework/testclient`,
so a request goes through routing, binding, validation and error rendering just
as it does in production.

## Layout

```
cmd/server/   composition, and nothing else
schemas/      the request and response models the API exposes
handlers/     the functions that answer requests
routers/      which handler answers which path
```

The dependencies point one way: routers know handlers, handlers know schemas,
and only `cmd/server` knows the routers, so each package can be tested on its
own. See https://muzak.dev/docs for the rest.
